column56:
Yes. You can see the compatibility between 80-bit floating points (long double in C) and 64-bit integer (long long int) 
with a code like this:<p><pre><code>  long double x0,x1,y0,y1;
  x0 = 18446744073709551615.0L; /* 2^64 - 1 */
  x1 = 18446744073709551616.0L; /* 2^64     */

  y0 = x0 + 1.0L;
  y1 = x1 + 1.0L;

  printf(&quot;%d\n&quot;, x0 == y0); /* false (with enough precision) */
  printf(&quot;%d\n&quot;, x1 == y1); /* true  (precision being lost ) */</code></pre>
